    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nDEFENCE SERVICES COMMAND ANDSTAFF COLLEGE (AMENDMENT)ACT, No. 29 OF 2013\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n[Certified on 08th July, 2013]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 2.50Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of July 12, 2013\n\n1Defence Services Command andStaff College (Amendment) Act, No. 29 of 2013\n\n2\u2014PL 007121\u20144090 (03/2013)\n\nShort title.\n\n[Certified on 08th July, 2013]\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 17/2012\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE DEFENCE SERVICES COMMAND AND STAFFCOLLEGE ACT, NO. 5 OF 2008\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Defence ServicesCommand and Staff College (Amendment) Act, No. 29 of2013.\n\n2.Section 7 of the Defence Services Command and StaffCollege Act, No. 5 of 2008 (hereinafter referred to as \u201ctheprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amended in subsection (1)of that section by the repeal of paragraph (f) of that subsectionand the substitution therefor, of the following paragraph:\u2014\n\n\u201c(f)the Vice-Chancellor of the General Sir JohnKotelawala Defence University;\u201d.\n\n3.Section 15 of the principal enactment is herebyamended in subsection (1) of that section by the repeal ofparagraph (b) of that subsection and the substitution therefor,of the following paragraph:\u2014\n\n\u201c(b)a representative nominated by the Vice-Chancellorof the General Sir John Kotelawala DefenceUniversity;\u201d.\n\n4.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAmendment ofsection 7 of theAct, No. 5 of2008.\n\nAmendment ofsection 15 of theprincipalenactment.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in caseof inconsistency.\n\n2Defence Services Command andStaff College (Amendment) Act, No. 29 of 2013"
